---
title: "SD-04 Open Pull Request and Mergeability Check (UML Sequence Diagram)"
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor U as Developer
  participant API as api.PullsHandler
  participant P as pulls.Service
  participant DB as store
  participant G as git.Repository
  participant EV as events.Bus
  participant Q as queue (worker)

  U->>API: POST /repos/alice/demo/pulls {base: main, head: feature}
  API->>P: Open(ctx, actor, repo, in)
  P->>G: ResolveCommit(feature) → headSha
  P->>DB: Tx: NextIssueNumber, INSERT issues(is_pull) + pull_requests(merge_status=unknown)
  P->>G: UpdateRef(refs/pull/7/head, headSha, "")
  P->>Q: Enqueue(pull.check_mergeable, pullID)
  P->>EV: Publish(pull.opened)
  P-->>API: Pull #7
  API-->>U: 201 Pull #7
  Q->>P: CheckMergeable(pullID)
  P->>G: MergeTree(baseTip, headSha)
  alt clean
    G-->>P: tree sha
    P->>DB: merge_status = clean
  else conflicts
    G-->>P: conflicting paths
    P->>DB: merge_status = conflict, conflict_files
  end
  P->>EV: Publish(pull.mergeability_changed)
  Note over EV: the trigger also receives pull.opened and starts PR pipelines
